text:
"A woman's eyes are like heaven,
    And her hair is like the golden grain;
Her lips are like the rose in May;
     And soft as she walks upon the plain."

My wife and me was wedded
In a long time agone;
We had seven little lasses
And one little young son;

Now it’s “May-o Mary,” and “Oh, dear!”

And “Run to mamma” anon;

But my day is busy all along,

With many a job to do!

And, as they say, “When the time came to take your leave.”

She said it like she meant it, but her lips didn’t move;

Her hands went up and down for emphasis while her eyes were wet;

For one last kiss with you before we had to part —

And I forgot everything save that it might be her heart!

Here the soul's heart lies concealed;
Every star would come there to rest;
There Love's power and passion dwell,
Our hearts are drawn by those who loved us once.
